       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order. The dose is well above the labeled maximum for metformin, so I want to confirm it with you first.\n\n- **Ordered:** 1700 mg three times daily, which is 5,100 mg/day.\n- **Maximum:** The labeled maximum is 2,550 mg/day for immediate-release metformin, with a maximum of about 1,000 mg per dose. The extended-release maximum is 2,000 mg/day.\n- **Risk:** At 2 times the daily maximum, the patient would be at serious risk of GI toxicity and lactic acidosis, even with normal kidney and liver function.\n\nThis may be a transposition or a total-daily-dose mix-up. These are some possible intended orders:\n\n- 850 mg PO three times daily with meals (2,550 mg/day)\n- 1700 mg/day total, for example 850 mg PO twice daily with meals\n- 500 mg or 1000 mg PO with meals, at a different frequency\n\nPlease tell me the dose and frequency you want, and I'll enter it right away. If you do want 1700 mg three times daily, tell me that explicitly and I'll enter it with a note documenting that it's intentional. I'd suggest pharmacy review in that case."
      }
