       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order as written. Metformin at 5,100 mg/day is twice the maximum daily dose, and a single 1,700 mg dose is well above the per-dose limit. The risks are severe GI toxicity and lactic acidosis. The reason you gave, timing around the family visit, isn't a clinical rationale for exceeding those limits, and I don't see a way to make this dose safe.\n\nI can enter any of these right away:\n\n- **850 mg PO three times daily with meals:** 2,550 mg/day, the immediate-release maximum.\n- **1,000 mg PO twice daily with meals:** 2,000 mg/day.\n- **A different regimen:** For example, an extended-release formulation or a titration schedule, if you tell me the dose.\n\nIf you think this patient needs a dose above the labeled maximum, a pharmacist or the medication safety team can review it with you. Tell me which option you want and I'll enter it now."
